BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Let's Walk!!
UID:event_316231596@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260913T043303Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260918T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260918T101500
SUMMARY:Eagle Rock Reservation
DESCRIPTION:Let's Walk!!\nJOIN US FOR A WALK. WE WALK AT A MODERATE PACE O
 N UNPAVED PATHS.\n\nWe will hike for about an hour - 3.5 miles. We will be
  walking on trails in the woods\, so appropriate footwear\, long pants & s
 ocks\, and bug spray.\n\nWill will meet at:\n[https://goo.gl/maps/7rRRTiXC
 ntdE1neD7](https://goo.gl/maps/7rRRTiXCntdE1neD7) Eagle Rock Trail Parking
  Lot by Kiosk#1\n\nIf you enter from Eagle Rock Way\, go pass the Highlawn
  and stay left. There will be a parking lot at the end of the curve to you
 r right.\n\nEagle Rock Reservation is 408 acres of hills\, streams\, and v
 alleys located on the borders of West Orange\, Verona\, and Montclair\, Ne
 w Jersey. Though located in the middle of the most densely populated count
 y in the most densely populated state in the country\, the Reservation is 
 mostly undeveloped and boasts an extensive trail system within its borders
 .\n\n**Please make sure to RSVP and arrive 5 minutes prior to start time.*
 *\n\nFOLLOW US ON INSTAGRAM - letswalkmeetup\n\nDisclaimer: If you join us
  for a hike\, please understand that you are responsible for your own prep
 aredness and well-being and will hold no one else liable in case of injury
  or mishap. Event will be canceled in the event of extreme weather.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lets-walkprogram/events/316231596/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260822T203035Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260822T203035Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Let's Walk!!
UID:event_316499392@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260913T043303Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260920T150000
SUMMARY:Walk at Grover Cleveland Park
DESCRIPTION:Let's Walk!!\n**MEETING TIME 9:30 AM**\n\nWe will meet near th
 e fishing pond entrance of the park\, close to Brookside Avenue and the bo
 at house/restrooms.\n**GPS location: 138 Brookside Ave\, Caldwell. Park on
  the street.**\n\nWe will walk for about 60-90 minutes at about a 3 miles/
 hour pace. The park has a paved path loop that is a little more than a mil
 e. Stay for as many loops as you like.\n\nGrover Cleveland Park in Caldwel
 l/Essex Fells celebrated its centennial in 2013. As the first county park 
 in western Essex County\, the site was originally selected for its natural
  beauty and its potential to provide a space for relaxation and recreation
 . It contains gentle rolling hills\, broad meadows and other environmental
 ly aesthetic features\n\n**Please arrive 5 minutes early\, so we can start
  on time.**\n\nFOLLOW US ON INSTAGRAM - letswalkmeetup\n\nDisclaimer: If y
 ou join us for a hike\, please understand that you are responsible for you
 r own preparedness and well-being and will hold no one else liable in case
  of injury or mishap. Event will be canceled in the event of extreme weath
 er.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lets-walkprogram/events/316499392/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260910T143303Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260910T143303Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Let's Walk!!
UID:event_316488259@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260913T043303Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260925T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260925T110000
SUMMARY:CEDAR GROVE PARK WALK  
DESCRIPTION:Let's Walk!!\nYou can **park** in the **Robert J. O'Toole Comm
 unity Center** parking lot located at **199 Fairview Ave\, Cedar Grove\, N
 J 07009**\n\n**Meet us under the gazebos** at the park directly across the
  street.\n\nWe will be walking the paved walking path that meanders over f
 oot bridges and past little “workout stations.”\n\nWe will walk about 
 3 - 4 miles. There are options to break off from the walk if you need to.\
 n\nBathrooms are available.\n\nCedar Grove Park is the newest addition to 
 the Essex County Park System\, formally dedicated on December 12\, 2016. A
 t 77 acres\, it is the fourth largest park in the county parks system. The
  park features the Robert J. O'Toole Community Center\, four bocce courts\
 , a farm themed playground area and three fitness stations along meanderin
 g walking paths.\n\nRain or extreme weather will cancel the event.\n\nPLEA
 SE ARRIVE 5 MINUTES PRIOR TO START TIME.\n\nDisclaimer: If you join us for
  a hike\, please understand that you are responsible for your own prepared
 ness and well-being and will hold no one else liable in case of injury or 
 mishap.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lets-walkprogram/events/316488259/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260909T193454Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T193454Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
